{
  "mcpServers": {
    "search": {
      "command": "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/uv",
      "args": [
        "run",
        "--script",
        "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/OpenExecutive/local/oe_ddg_search.py"
      ]
    }
  },
  "filters": {
    "access_control": {
      "deny_patterns": [
        "*__delete_*",
        "*__drop_*",
        "*__destroy_*",
        "*__remove_*"
      ],
      "deny": [],
      "allow_servers": []
    },
    "load_control": {
      "deny_url_patterns": [
        "http://*"
      ],
      "allow_url_patterns": []
    },
    "similarity_threshold": 0.3
  },
  "_comment": "Local-only search+read for a no-API-key deployment. Open Executive's builtin web_search is Anthropic's SERVER-side tool and is stripped by providers/feature_gate.py before reaching a local model; MCP tools arrive as client tools with input_schema and survive. One server only: oe_ddg_search.py provides search, news AND read. The official mcp-server-fetch is deliberately NOT configured -- it would hand the model page content without a source marker, which is exactly the hole that let it cite nine pages it never opened. Absolute command paths on purpose: the MCP stdio client gives children only a fixed env allowlist, so ~/.local/bin is not guaranteed on PATH."
}
